,title,link,text,language,family
0,Nisga'a language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nisga'a_language,"January 25, 2026 - Nisga’a (also Nisg̱a’a, Nass, Nisgha, Nishka, Niska, Nishga, Nisqa’a) is an indigenous language of northwestern British Columbia. It is a part of the language family generally called Tsimshianic, although some Nisga'a people resent the precedence the term gives to Coast Tsimshian.",Nisga’a,Tsimshian
1,Nisga'a | The Canadian Encyclopedia,https://thecanadianencyclopedia.ca/en/article/nisgaa,"Drumming and traditional dances are also important to Nisga’a culture. Music and dance are performed for entertainment, such as at festivals like the Nisga’a new year, Hobiyee (held every February), or for spiritual purposes during certain rituals.",Nisga’a,Tsimshian
2,Ts'msyen (Tsimshian) | The Canadian Encyclopedia,https://thecanadianencyclopedia.ca/en/article/tsimshian,"In 1988, the Ts’msyen created the Tsimshian Tribal Council. It represented seven Ts’msyen bands in negotiations with the British Columbia and federal governments. These bands included Kitselas, Kitsumkalum, Gitga’at, Kitasoo, Metlakatla, Lax Kw’alaams and Gitxa’ala.",Nisga’a,Tsimshian
3,Tsimshian | American Museum of Natural History,https://www.amnh.org/exhibitions/permanent/northwest-coast/tsimshian,"Despite the importance of songs, in the past, the Tsimshian had few musical instruments. The principal ones were drums, rattles, and whistles—instruments still in use today.",Nisga’a,Tsimshian
4,NISGA'A SONG & DANCE!: nudenisgaa_79 — LiveJournal,https://nudenisgaa-79.livejournal.com/10117.html,"and right up to when i had started, we had to battle with a few indaviduals to Have one'z Dance regalia blessed in the church. it wasn't until after 1990, when Hlayanwil started up nisga'a song & dance with the Misaak dancerz, making & giving them songs to use.",Nisga’a,Tsimshian
5,"Mike Dangeli, Nisga'a, Tlingit, Tsimshian Products - Native Northwest",https://nativenorthwest.com/mike-dangeli-nisgaa-tlingit-tsimshian/,"Mike Dangeli, Nisga'a, Tlingit, Tsimshian · Mike Dangeli, Nisga'a, Tlingit, Tsimshian ·",Nisga’a,Tsimshian
6,Home of the Nisga'a Nation - song and lyrics by Lowry Olafson | Spotify,https://open.spotify.com/track/6qt3N8gjBx6iG4gRtLtcfU,"Home of the Nisga'a Nation · Song · Lowry Olafson•My Dog Ate My Homework•2009•2:56•1,116 · Sign in to see lyrics and listen to the full track · Log inSign up · Artist · Lowry Olafson · RecommendedBased on this song · TreasureLuther Wright & The Wrongs ·",Nisga’a,Tsimshian
7,Haida / Tsimshian / Haisla / Nisga’a - Make A Future,https://www.makeafuture.ca/bc-regions/haida-tsimshian-haisla-nisgaa/,"May 28, 2025 - In addition to band-operated schools, there provincially operated First Nations Schools in the Nisga’a Villages of Gitwinksihlk and New Aiyansh operating out of School District #92 (Nisga’a).",Nisga’a,Tsimshian
8,Indigenous Language Families: Tsimshian languages,https://www150.statcan.gc.ca/n1/pub/41-20-0002/412000022025009-eng.htm,"March 31, 2025 - This report is part of a series on Indigenous language families in Canada, using data from the 2021 Census of Population. It provides an overview of the vitality, acquisition and use of Indigenous languages that belong to the Tsimshian language family. The following languages are covered: Gitxsan (Gitksan), Nisga'a and Tsimshian.",Nisga’a,Tsimshian
9,"Tlingit, Haida, Eyak, & Tsimshian Culture in Alaska | Travel Alaska",https://www.travelalaska.com/things-to-do/alaska-native-culture/cultures/tlingit-haida-eyak-tsimshian,"In Sitka, experience the drumming and hear traditional stories shared by the Sheet'ka Kwaan Naa Kahidi Dancers at the Sheet'ka Kwaan Naa Kahidi Community House. The Sealaska Heritage Institute in Juneau continues the arts, cultural, and language traditions of the Tlingit, Haida, and Tsimshian peoples through workshops, classes, monumental art, and collections.",Nisga’a,Tsimshian
